    {
      "case": "relation load, one level",
      "arm": "kysely",
      "why": "the nested `bigint` ids come back through a float64, for the same reason as drizzle and from a different API: `jsonArrayFrom` aggregates children with `json_agg` and the result arrives as JSON, so `JSON.parse` turns an id past 2^53 into the nearest double before anything types it. It returns a `number`, not even a wrong `bigint`. pg-prime emits `id::text` INSIDE `json_build_object` and decodes it through the column’s codec, which is why its column is exact — and which is also extra work this comparison charges it for. Measured 2026-08-29 against kysely 0.29.5.",
